    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Half a century ago, a boy in Britain had never thought that a dream of his would drive him to spend decades in a foreign country."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "That boy was William Lindsay. When in primary school, he loved studying maps. The "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "saw-tooth",
            "zh": "锯齿般的"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " line in China caught his eye. He decided to visit the line, that is, the Great Wall of China."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Driven by this dream, Lindsay set off on his Great Wall journey in 1984. However, he "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "obviously",
            "ref": "v-obviously"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "underestimated",
            "ref": "v-underestimate"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " its difficulty. Only a few days later, he became ill and had to give up his plan. After returning to Britain, he began to exercise more often. He even learnt some basic Chinese."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "With full preparation, Lindsay set off again in 1987. Altogether, the hike took him about 160 days. This tall man "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "encountered",
            "ref": "v-encounter"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " trouble when he was found walking alone along the Yulin Great Wall in Shaanxi. “Where is he from? What is he doing here?” the local villagers wondered. Finally, the police came to investigate. Lindsay tried to explain his love for the Wall, but without success. At last, he had to leave."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Nothing could stop his "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "willful",
            "ref": "v-willful"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " heart. A few days later, Lindsay continued his journey from Inner Mongolia. After many, many difficult days of hiking along the Great Wall, he finally arrived at Shanhaiguan, a major pass at the eastern end of the Wall and the end of his great journey."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Through this trip, Lindsay developed a deeper understanding of the Great Wall. Since then, he has made great efforts to protect it. In 1988, he organised more than 120 volunteers to pick up litter on the Great Wall. Lindsay soon realised the difficulty of collecting all the trash on the Wall. He began giving lectures around the country and began looking for more volunteers."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p7",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "During Lindsay’s Great Wall hike, he met with his Miss Right, a Chinese girl from Xi’an. They got married in 1988. Lindsay’s wife and two sons have now also joined him in protecting the Great Wall. The British man said he would spend his remaining years in China—for his family and for the Wall."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
